trenova-db: Trenova's database: migrations and reference seeds.

Usage: trenova-db [flags] <command> [arguments]

Run trenova-db with no command in a terminal to open the console.

Commands:
  up                migrate, then apply seeds: the deploy step
  migrate up        apply pending migrations
  migrate plan      show what migrate up would do
  migrate status    list migrations with their state
  migrate history   list applied migrations
  migrate create    write a new migration file
  migrate squash    replace applied migrations with one baseline
  migrate stamp     write the schema version file, or check it
  migrate check     check ordering and checksums
  migrate lint      lint pending migrations
  migrate baseline  record migrations up to version as applied
  migrate repair    accept the current checksum of a changed migration
  seed apply        apply seeds that changed, or the named ones
  seed plan         show which seeds would run and why
  seed status       list seeds with their state
  seed prune        delete records of seeds no longer registered
  reset             recreate the database from the current template
  template          list template databases
  template build    build the current template
  template prune    drop stale templates
  doctor            check the database, its settings and what holds locks
  version           print the version
  help [command]    show help for a command

Global flags, before or after the command:
  -json            write JSON: one document per result, one line per event
  -no-color        do not colour output (NO_COLOR also works)
  -plain           write plain text even in a terminal
  -yes             answer yes to confirmations
  -yes-production  allow destructive commands on a production database

Exit codes: 0 ok, 1 failure, 2 usage or refusal, 3 a check found problems.
